sequenceDiagram
    %% Comments flow 1 of 4 — Load
    %% Entering the reader: fetch the conversation and draw it on the page.
    %% Participants map to:
    %%   MS  src/screens/ManuscriptScreen.js
    %%   ST  src/stores/commentsStore.js
    %%   API src/services/commentsService.js
    %%   JS  src/components/PdfViewer.js
    %%   NV  ios/RNPdfViewer.swift (RNPdfView)
    %%   SH  ios/CommentSheetView.swift
    %% Props and events between NV and JS pass through the
    %% RCT_EXPORT_VIEW_PROPERTY declarations in ios/RNPdfViewer.m.
    autonumber
    actor R as Reader
    participant MS as ManuscriptScreen.js
    participant ST as commentsStore
    participant API as commentsService
    participant SRV as Server
    participant JS as PdfViewer.js
    participant NV as RNPdfView
    participant SH as CommentSheetView

    R->>MS: navigate to ManuscriptScreen
    MS->>MS: resolve roomId from shelf + last-used preference
    Note over MS: Solo book has no roomId,<br/>so no conversation to fetch

    MS->>ST: loadComments(roomId, bookId)
    ST->>API: fetchBookComments(roomId, bookId)
    API->>SRV: GET /room/{roomId}/book/{bookId}/comments
    SRV-->>API: 200 threads + locked_count + unlocked_unread_count
    Note over SRV: Spoiler rule applied server-side.<br/>Pages ahead of the reader arrive<br/>as a bare locked_count
    API-->>ST: status, response
    ST->>ST: map toThread, sortThreads by page then createdAt
    ST-->>MS: byBook updated

    MS->>MS: nativeThreads useMemo
    MS->>JS: threads, hasRoom, roomName, unreadTotal, lockedCount
    JS->>NV: props via RCT_EXPORT_VIEW_PROPERTY

    NV->>NV: parsedThreads = map ReaderThread(NSDictionary)
    NV->>NV: scrubber.commentPages = unique pages
    NV->>NV: scheduleOverlayRefresh, 50ms debounce
    NV->>SH: update(threads, roomName, submitting)
    Note over SH: Stores data, then guards on isOpen.<br/>Closed sheet stays current, does not render

    NV->>NV: refreshOverlays
    Note over NV: Per thread: skip if fileHash differs from<br/>documentHash, else findString the anchor text<br/>or fall back to normalized bounds
    NV->>R: highlights + gutter dots + scrubber ticks
